%description:

Tcp.initialSsthresh:invalid -- a threshold of 0 stops the run with an error.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "1 to 4294967295".

The classes: high (the default 4294967295, "arbitrarily high"), low (a value that slow start
reaches), invalid (0, or above 4294967295). The code: the algorithms read it at the start
(TcpClassicAlgorithmBase, TcpTahoe, TcpVegas, TcpWestwood), and TcpAlgorithmBase checks it.

Host under test: host1, whose algorithm reads the threshold at the open. Observation: the
error, and the exit code of the run.

%# parameter: Tcp.initialSsthresh
%# class: invalid
%# value: 0
%# key: *.host1.tcp.initialSsthresh
%# expected-result: PASS

%activity:
EV << "TcpInitialSsthreshInvalid compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.initialSsthresh = 0    # the parameter under test
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%exitcode: 1

%contains-regex: stderr
initialSsthresh must be 1 to 4294967295, but it is 0
